# Drive the robot straight ahead for a given distance.
#
# An ACTION is the right pattern here, and neither a topic nor a service would do:
#   * a topic cannot report whether the move finished,
#   * a service would block the caller for the whole drive and could not be cancelled
#     halfway, nor report progress.
# Actions are what Navigation2 itself uses for "go to this pose" -- the same reason
# applies: the task takes seconds, the caller wants progress, and it must be
# abortable.
#
# An action definition has THREE parts separated by '---': goal, result, feedback.

# ---------- GOAL: sent once by the client to start the task ----------
float64 distance      # metres to travel; must be > 0
float64 speed         # m/s; clamped by the server to its safety limit
---
# ---------- RESULT: sent once when the task ends (success, abort or cancel) ----------
float64 distance_travelled   # how far we actually got [m]
bool success
string message
---
# ---------- FEEDBACK: streamed repeatedly while the task runs ----------
float64 distance_travelled   # [m]
float64 percent_complete     # 0-100
